---
import PhotoPlaceholder from '../PhotoPlaceholder.astro';
import VisionFigure from '../VisionFigure.astro';
import SectionHead from '../SectionHead.astro';
---

<section class="band-cream section">
  <SectionHead num="9 / 14 — People" heading="Twenty-four thousand a year." />

  <div class="container-page">
    <PhotoPlaceholder
      description="A kitchen table, a stack of bills, a calendar. Or a parent handing keys back at a used-car lot. The household ledger image — the moment a family realizes what a second car actually costs them."
    />
  </div>

  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="vision-prose">
      <p>
        AAA has been publishing an annual report on the cost of car ownership for fifty years. The
        2025 number, all-in — fuel, insurance, maintenance, depreciation, payment, registration — is
        just over <strong>$12,000 per car</strong> for the average sedan. A two-car household, which is
        the average household in Clark County, runs
        <strong>$24,000 a year</strong> on transportation alone. That is roughly a quarter of the median
        Clark County paycheck. Most of it leaves Nevada the moment it's spent: out-of-state insurers,
        oil majors, automakers, finance companies headquartered in Connecticut and Texas and Detroit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container-page">
    <VisionFigure num="9" title="Where one car's $12,000 a year goes">
      <div class="cost-chart">
        <div class="cost-bar-wrap">
          <div class="cost-label">One car<em>$12,000 / yr</em></div>
          <div>
            <div
              class="cost-bar"
              role="img"
              aria-label="One car: $12,000 per year, broken down as $2,400 fuel, $2,000 insurance, $4,400 payment, $1,400 maintenance, $1,800 depreciation"
            >
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-fuel" style="flex: 2.4;">$2,400</div>
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-ins" style="flex: 2.0;">$2,000</div>
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-pay" style="flex: 4.4;">$4,400</div>
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-maint" style="flex: 1.4;">$1,400</div>
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-dep" style="flex: 1.8;">$1,800</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cost-bar-wrap">
          <div class="cost-label">Two cars<em>$24,000 / yr</em></div>
          <div>
            <div
              class="cost-bar"
              role="img"
              aria-label="Two cars: $24,000 per year, broken down as $4,800 fuel, $4,000 insurance, $8,800 payment, $2,800 maintenance, $3,600 depreciation"
            >
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-fuel" style="flex: 2.4;">$4,800</div>
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-ins" style="flex: 2.0;">$4,000</div>
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-pay" style="flex: 4.4;">$8,800</div>
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-maint" style="flex: 1.4;">$2,800</div>
              <div class="cost-seg cost-s-dep" style="flex: 1.8;">$3,600</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cost-legend">
          <span class="cost-legend-item"><span class="cost-swatch cost-s-fuel"></span> Fuel</span>
          <span class="cost-legend-item"
            ><span class="cost-swatch cost-s-ins"></span> Insurance</span
          >
          <span class="cost-legend-item"
            ><span class="cost-swatch cost-s-pay"></span> Payment / financing</span
          >
          <span class="cost-legend-item"
            ><span class="cost-swatch cost-s-maint"></span> Maintenance</span
          >
          <span class="cost-legend-item"
            ><span class="cost-swatch cost-s-dep"></span> Depreciation</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <Fragment slot="caption">
        AAA's annual ownership-cost study. The actual cost is spread across categories most
        households never add up.
      </Fragment>
    </VisionFigure>
  </div>

  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="vision-prose">
      <p>
        The Valley we're building doesn't get rid of cars. It makes the second car optional for
        households that don't need one — which, with real bus service, a protected bike network, and
        walkable neighborhoods, is most of them. The household that drops a second car keeps roughly <span
          class="inline-highlight">$1,000 a month</span
        >. That is a college fund, a down payment, a real vacation, an emergency cushion. It also
        doesn't disappear into national insurance and oil supply chains; it stays in the local
        economy, paying rent, buying groceries, supporting Las&nbsp;Vegas businesses that pay
        Las&nbsp;Vegas wages.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is the part of the vision that is least about transit and most about households.
        Transportation is the second-largest expense the average American family carries, after
        housing. Reducing it is the most direct way the Valley can make itself more affordable to
        its own residents — without subsidizing developers, without building a single new highway,
        without doing anything that requires anyone to leave a house they love.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cost-chart {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cost-bar-wrap {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .cost-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .cost-label em {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .cost-bar {
    display: flex;
    height: 36px;
  }
  .cost-seg {
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-right: 2px solid var(--color-paper);
  }
  .cost-seg:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }
  .cost-s-fuel {
    background: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .cost-s-ins {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 75%, var(--color-accent));
  }
  .cost-s-pay {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 50%, var(--color-accent));
  }
  .cost-s-maint {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 25%, var(--color-accent));
  }
  .cost-s-dep {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    /* Paper on accent is 3.64:1 — under AA. Flip to ink only on the
       lightest segment; the darker mixes keep paper text. */
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .cost-legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--vp-text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .cost-legend-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .cost-swatch {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    display: inline-block;
  }
</style>
